;; writing-patterns.edn — the paper's house style as executable patterns.
;; Each entry is one rewrite rule with a REAL exemplar from this paper's own
;; revision history. Two sources: :house = established by operator ruling
;; during the 2026-08-08/09 passes; :captured = extracted from a Joe edit
;; during proofing (the de-AI-ifying loop; see PATTERNS.md).
;;
;; Schema per pattern:
;;   :id        kebab keyword
;;   :status    :house | :candidate | :retired
;;   :trigger   what to look for (greppable cues or a described smell)
;;   :before    verbatim exemplar as it stood
;;   :after     verbatim exemplar as ruled
;;   :rule      the transformation, stated generally
;;   :why       one line
;;   :source    where the ruling happened

{:updated "2026-08-09"
 :patterns
 [{:id :timeless-register
   :status :house
   :trigger "narrative past tense about the writing/research process; 'initially',
             'we then realised', 'reason not recorded', dates in body prose"
   :before "seven months of exploration in this substrate family before the
            selection layer existed encountered nothing resembling the valley
            configuration"
   :after "its scope is thirty runs, two geometries, and one vocabulary of
           twelve operators; it is not a claim about rule-rewriting lattices
           generally"
   :rule "State what is and what was measured; never narrate the project's
          history in the paper's voice."
   :why "Elapsed time and process anecdotes are not assessable evidence."
   :source "part3 probes pass, ruling 2026-08-09"}

  {:id :no-self-narration
   :status :house
   :trigger "'we retain', 'we avoid the phrase', 'we do not claim' used to
             manage the reader rather than scope a result; sentences about the
             paper rather than the system"
   :before "A reader should therefore not expect Part~II's causal coordinate
            to explain Part~III's outcomes, and the paper never asks it to."
   :after "(sentence deleted; the seam statement already carries it)"
   :rule "Say the fact once; never add a sentence telling the reader how to
          read the fact."
   :why "Editorial self-narration is noise after the claim is stated."
   :source "scope-seam paragraph, ruling 2026-08-09 ('tying themselves in
            knots to state a negative fact, why bother')"}

  {:id :state-the-positive
   :status :house
   :trigger "claims of the form 'X without Y' / 'does not reproduce' /
             'fails to' where what actually happens is known and describable"
   :before "undirected noise prevents freezing without reproducing the found
            configuration's structure"
   :after "what it holds looks different: a foam of small frozen islands amid
           changing surroundings, against the extended frozen and changing
           regions of the found configuration; the measured difference is
           frozen fraction, 0.3 against 0.08"
   :rule "Replace a negative claim with a description of what each state IS,
          plus the measured difference."
   :why "Negatives hide the phenomenon; the foam was more interesting than
         the non-reproduction."
   :source "Fork 4 ruling 2026-08-09 ('states a negative... what that
            structure actually *is*')"}

  {:id :concrete-operation
   :status :house
   :trigger "nominalizations and insider metaphors standing in for an
             operation: 'consumed an axis', 'cuts the currency', named
             constructions used before body-prose definition"
   :before "It cuts the \\emph{currency} of the read, not the read."
   :after "the difference is when each frozen field is captured: the ablated
           control freezes each branch's phenotype at the fork, so the
           perturbed branch's frozen field contains the flip; the gamma-dial
           reads a reference field identical in both branches"
   :rule "Unpack every compressed phrase into the operation it names, with
          its parameters, before (or instead of) using the compression."
   :why "A reader cannot reconstruct referents the section never supplies."
   :source "part2 audit + codex proposals, applied 2026-08-09"}

  {:id :measured-scope
   :status :house
   :trigger "'no X exists', 'cannot', 'did not become', universal negatives
             whose evidence is a finite test set"
   :before "The search did not become autonomous"
   :after "The search was not endogenous---the apparatus varied the
           parameters and scored the runs from outside"
   :rule "Scope every negative to what was tested, and name the axis on which
          the thing failed rather than a vaguer stronger one."
   :why "'We found no X' survives review; 'there is no X' invites refutation
         (and Droste 2013 later refuted the unscoped reading)."
   :source "rulings 2026-08-08/09, incl. 'not endogenous' and 'no tested
            local quantity'"}

  {:id :titles-are-claims
   :status :house
   :trigger "section titles that name territory ('Related Constructions',
             'Analysis', 'Discussion of X')"
   :before "\\section{Related Constructions}"
   :after "\\section{Related Work: A New Operator Family Among Familiar
           Phenomena}"
   :rule "Every numbered section title states the section's claim. Part
          titles may name objects (The Permutation Core; Exotypes)."
   :why "The TOC carries the argument."
   :source "memory paper-toc-carries-argument; fork-5 rulings"}

  {:id :name-before-use
   :status :house
   :trigger "a term first appearing in a caption or later section: check
             river, ridge, dwell, foam, exotype, pinned, arm"
   :before "(the river defined only inside a figure caption; 'the ridge'
            first appearing in a caption)"
   :after "body prose defines the operation and names it before any caption
           or later section uses it"
   :rule "Define and name every construct in body prose at first use;
          captions may repeat but never introduce."
   :why "Captions are read out of order; prose is the contract."
   :source "part2/part3 audits, applied 2026-08-09"}

  {:id :anchor-numbers
   :status :house
   :trigger "a threshold or constant appearing exactly once with no stated
             provenance (the '135' test: grep any bare number in a claim)"
   :before "fields can remain mobile and propagate damage at effective
            diversities well above $135$ without mutation"
   :after "at sustained diversities above $135$ distinct rules---the highest
           diversity any mechanism of the original survey reaches without
           replacement mutation or a held genotype (Figure 11, grey band;
           Supplement 1, Box 12)"
   :rule "Every number in a claim names its referent and its source; verify
          the referent against the data, not against memory."
   :why "Joe's check found the audit's own gloss of 135 was wrong; the data
         said something sharper."
   :source "Fork 2 ruling 2026-08-09"}

  {:id :full-name-at-definition
   :status :captured
   :trigger "a term of art introduced by its bare short form: 'An operator is
             defined...' where the paper's term is 'rule-rewriting operator';
             check definitional sentences for river, gate, exotype, arm too"
   :before "An operator is defined by a permutation $\sig$ of the eight
            truth-table positions"
   :after "A rule-rewriting operator is defined by a permutation $\sig$ of
           the eight truth-table positions"
   :rule "Definition sites and first uses carry the full term of art; bare
          short forms are for bound subsequent uses only."
   :why "Joe, rocket record 2: 'we should call this a rule rewriting
         operator, not just an operator.'"
   :source "rocket 2026-08-10; applied at abstract + outline 1.1.1; 1.1.2
            left bare (bound by 1.1.1's definition one line above)"}

 {:id :false-instead
   :status :captured
   :trigger "'instead'/'rather' presenting a different measurement or question
             as if it answered the one just declined; test: are the two items
             genuinely alternative answers to the same question?"
   :before "we find no critical point. We measure instead how far the effect
            of a single-cell change travels"
   :after "we find no critical point. We then expand the class of automata
           architectures, and examine criticality by measuring how far the
           effect of a single-cell change travels"
   :rule "Reserve contrastive connectives for genuine alternatives. And when
          removing a false one, deleting the connective is the lesser fix:
          supply the actual move that makes the next measurement follow
          (what changed, and what question it now serves)."
   :why "Joe, rocket: 'that is not really an instead, that is just measuring
         something different'; then his hand edit refined the minimal
         deletion into a statement of the move itself."
   :source "rocket 2026-08-10 + hand-edit refinement (the first captured
            wysiwyg-side ruling); swept 6 other instances, all genuine
            contrasts, kept"}

 {:id :frame-the-question
   :status :captured
   :trigger "a transition (especially across part boundaries) that opens with
             a negative result; also definite articles presupposing referents
             not yet introduced in that unit ('the coexisting state')"
   :before "Finally, individual cells cannot choose between operators from
            local observation: ..."
   :after "Finally, we make the operator assignment itself a per-cell
           heritable state---an exotype---and ask whether local dynamics
           alone can find and hold the regime in which frozen and changing
           regions coexist... Within the tested family it cannot: ..."
   :rule "State the question a stretch of negatives answers before the
          negatives; each unit (abstract, intro, part) introduces its own
          referents."
   :why "Joe, rocket: 'starting with a negative result and not
         contextualizing the question... decontextualized and just very
         hard to follow because there is no framing.'"
   :source "rocket 2026-08-10; sweep: intro third-finding and outline 1.3
            already frame first — the abstract was the one unframed bridge"}

 {:id :credit-the-interaction
   :status :captured
   :trigger "apparatus or policy described as the finder/actor where the
             actual process was operator-in-the-loop; also results appearing
             agentless ('the local interventions that do prevent freezing')"
   :before "a regime an external selection policy does find ... The local
            interventions that do prevent freezing hold a foam"
   :after "a regime that an external selection policy helped us find
           interactively ... However, we constructed local interventions
           that do prevent freezing"
   :rule "Name the actual search process (who/what, and that it was
          interactive when it was) and claim constructed things as
          constructed."
   :why "Joe's hand edit; matches the intro's existing honesty ('varying it
         from outside, between runs, is how the coexistence examples were
         found') and the not-endogenous ruling in [[measured-scope]]."
   :source "hand edit 2026-08-10; sweep: body already conforms, abstract was
            the site"}

 {:id :scoped-negative-names-its-subject
   :status :captured
   :trigger "a scoped negative whose subject is a pronoun: 'it cannot',
             'this fails', 'none do' — name the mechanism, the family, and
             the criterion instead"
   :before "Within the tested family it cannot: the relevant local field
            decorrelates..."
   :after "Within the tested family of exotypes, local selection was not
           able to recover the observed behaviour. The relevant local field
           decorrelates..."
   :rule "A negative claim names its subject (which mechanism), its scope
          (which family), and its criterion (recover what) — and stands as
          its own sentence rather than a colon-chain head."
   :why "Joe's hand edit refining the frame-the-question rewrite; sharpens
         [[measured-scope]] from 'scope the negative' to 'name all three
         parts of it'."
   :source "hand edit 2026-08-10; sweep: no other bare-pronoun negatives
            remain"}

 {:id :verdict-not-litany
   :status :captured
   :trigger "in the abstract: a multi-clause chain of negative evidence
             following an already-stated verdict; reads as a litany of
             failures and duplicates the intro's detail"
   :before "...was not able to recover the observed behaviour. The relevant
            local field decorrelates in about six steps, ...; copying rules
            across phase boundaries accelerates...; and although... no
            locally computable quantity we tested identifies that outcome.
            However, we constructed..."
   :after "...was not able to recover the observed behaviour. However, we
           constructed..."
   :rule "The abstract carries verdicts; the evidence chains behind a
          negative verdict live in the introduction and the sections that
          contextualize them. (Positive core results may keep their clauses:
          the Part II chain states the paper's deltas.)"
   :why "Joe, rocket: 'by its very length reads as a litany of failures...
         go directly from not being able to recover the observed behavior
         to the construction of local interventions.'"
   :source "rocket 2026-08-10; the cut material verified present in the
            intro third-finding and Part III body"}

 {:id :evidence-carries-inspiration
   :status :house
   :trigger "a result that exists because a specific work suggested the
             design, stated without that work's citation"
   :before "A one-sided rule (write only into long-settled cells) holds a
            mixed state..."
   :after "A one-sided rule in the design class of \\textcite{droste2013analytical}
           ---write only into long-settled cells---holds a mixed state..."
   :rule "When the literature directed the experiment, the sentence reporting
          it cites the direction."
   :why "Provenance is part of the finding."
   :source "outline 1.3.5/1.3.6 ruling 2026-08-09"}]}
